#: ../../../ros2_spawn_model.md:1
msgid "Spawn a Gazebo model from ROS 2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_spawn_model.md:3
msgid ""
"Gazebo will spawn all the models included in the provided world file at "
"startup. Additionally, it's possible to spawn new models at any time. To do "
"so using ROS we have provided the following mechanisms:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_spawn_model.md:7
msgid "Spawn a model using the launch file included in `ros_gz_sim`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_spawn_model.md:9
msgid ""
"The package `ros_gz_sim` contains a launch file named `gz_spawn_model.launch."
"py`. You can use it to spawn a new model into an existing simulation. Here's "
"an example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_spawn_model.md:13
msgid ""
"ros2 launch ros_gz_sim gz_spawn_model.launch.py world:=empty file:=$(ros2 "
"pkg prefix --share ros_gz_sim_demos)/models/vehicle/model.sdf entity_name:"
"=my_vehicle x:=5.0 y:=5.0 z:=0.5\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_spawn_model.md:17
msgid ""
"Check [this block](https://github.com/gazebosim/ros_gz/blob/"
"cadae1c8323a74395c09a37e3de4c669c8c09d4f/ros_gz_sim/launch/"
"ros_gz_spawn_model.launch.py#L33-L44) from the source code to know all the "
"different parameters accepted by this launch file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_spawn_model.md:21
msgid "Spawn a model from a custom launch file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_spawn_model.md:23
msgid ""
"It's also possible to spawn the model from your custom launch file. For that "
"purpose we have created the `<gz_spawn_model/>` tag that can be used from "
"you XML or YAML launch file. In this case, the arguments are passed as "
"attributes within this tag. Here's an example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_spawn_model.md:28
msgid ""
"<launch>\n"
"  <arg name=\"world\" default=\"\" />\n"
"  <arg name=\"file\" default=\"\" />\n"
"  <arg name=\"model_string\" default=\"\" />\n"
"  <arg name=\"topic\" default=\"\" />\n"
"  <arg name=\"entity_name\" default=\"\" />\n"
"  <arg name=\"allow_renaming\" default=\"False\" />\n"
"  <arg name=\"x\" default=\"\" />\n"
"  <arg name=\"y\" default=\"\" />\n"
"  <arg name=\"z\" default=\"\" />\n"
"  <arg name=\"roll\" default=\"\" />\n"
"  <arg name=\"pitch\" default=\"\" />\n"
"  <arg name=\"yaw\" default=\"\" />\n"
"  <gz_spawn_model \n"
"    world=\"$(var world)\"\n"
"    file=\"$(var file)\"\n"
"    model_string=\"$(var model_string)\"\n"
"    topic=\"$(var topic)\"\n"
"    entity_name=\"$(var entity_name)\"\n"
"    allow_renaming=\"$(var allow_renaming)\"\n"
"    x=\"$(var x)\"\n"
"    y=\"$(var y)\"\n"
"    z=\"$(var z)\"\n"
"    roll=\"$(var roll)\"\n"
"    pitch=\"$(var pitch)\"\n"
"    yaw=\"$(var yaw)\">\n"
"  </gz_spawn_model>\n"
"</launch>\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_spawn_model.md:59
msgid ""
"In this case the `<gz_spawn_model>` parameters are read from the command "
"line. That's an option but not strictly necessary as you could decide to "
"hardcode some of the values or not even use all of the parameters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_spawn_model.md:64
msgid "Spawning a model alongside launching ros_gz_bridge"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_spawn_model.md:66
msgid ""
"An example launch file for XML can be viewed [here](https://github.com/"
"gazebosim/ros_gz/blob/jazzy/ros_gz_sim/launch/ros_gz_spawn_model.launch) An "
"example launch file for Python can be viewed [here](https://github.com/"
"gazebosim/ros_gz/blob/jazzy/ros_gz_sim/launch/ros_gz_spawn_model.launch.py)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_spawn_model.md:69
msgid ""
"Example command for directly using these launch files from the terminal:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_spawn_model.md:70
msgid ""
"ros2 launch ros_gz_sim ros_gz_spawn_model.launch.py world:=empty file:"
"=$(ros2 pkg prefix --share ros_gz_sim_demos)/models/vehicle/model.sdf "
"entity_name:=my_vehicle x:=5.0 y:=5.0 z:=0.5 bridge_name:=ros_gz_bridge "
"config_file:=<path_to_your_YAML_file>\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_spawn_model.md:74
msgid "More info about `ros_gz_bridge` can be viewed [here](ros2_integration)."
msgstr ""
